Thanks.', '英语2/语法基础第十节-定从1.pdf', 47, true, 41, null),
  ('2d70f877-62a7-52d1-89c1-208708b5ad11', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '绝对明确 2. 相对明确 作用 修饰限定先行词，不能省 略，影响表意 补充说明先行词，可以省 略，不影响 非限制性定语从句总结 6', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 5, true, 42, null),
  ('6bf4fa30-27eb-5070-90ec-8e380f3d0cf0', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.【绝对明确】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 43, null),
  ('6b9a9709-1570-5323-8d6f-34129fbf39f2', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'but two years ago Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have any physical product at all.【绝对明确】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 44, null),
  ('92bc6616-3849-532c-95cf-663ea7e7ca80', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty. 【相对明确-短期投资者】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 45, null),
  ('f1e6c7eb-0b93-5e4d-8bc0-4f4ae9941041', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'they''ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another big concern for colleges. 【相对明确-学费】 非限制性定语从句阅读方式-分清主从句，意群，谁跟谁并列 7 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers. 在爱荷华州，这一表态并未得到广泛认同。该州田野上风力发电机星罗棋布，风电已占全州发电量的 36%。科技巨头（如微软）正因清洁能源的充沛供应而纷纷选址于此，为其数据中心提供动力支持。 第一步：找出所有动词 did not play，dot，provide，are being attracted， to power 第二步：非谓语动词词组=起点+终点（前） 起点：to do；doing；done 终点=下一个标点符号前；下一个连接词前；下一 个动词前 to power their data centers. 第三步：一个连词+搭配一个动词+终点（下一个 标点符号；下一个连接词；下一个动词）', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 6, true, 46, null),
  ('f7240de3-7d59-5155-9ff9-180cbe137c6e', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'where wind turbines .... electricity generation', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 7, true, 47, null),
  ('ec603ac7-1d79-5b32-a631-fcff090e620b', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'where tech giants.... clean energy 解决三个问题①形式中判断是非限制性定从 ②分清楚句子层次，主 从句，谁跟谁并列③复现意群 ④学有余力者，翻译 8 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 问题一：复现意群？？？ 上下义复现【概括+具体】：2组词 同义复现/替换：1组词 指代复现：1组 非限制性定从，大于8个字，所以翻译时候独立成句 9 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 上下义复现【概括+具体】：clean energy-wind；tech giants-Microsoft 同义复现/替换：provide electricity=to power 指代复现： tech giants-their 翻译：非限制性定从，大于8个字，所以翻译时候独立成句 10 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 但这一说法在爱荷华州并不受许多民众认可。在该州，风力发电机遍布田野，风能供应全州 36% 的 发电量；也正是在该州，充足的清洁能源吸引了微软这类科技巨头入驻，为它们的数据中心供 电。 真题演练六：风能供电，为科技巨头数据中心供电，与这个方向更 贴近 11 President Trump has underlined fossil fuels——especially coal——as the path to economic growth. In a recent speech in Iowa，he dismissed wind power as an unreliable energy source. But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 7, true, 48, null),
  ('d7f47969-3e9c-53f9-bc8c-98a185d25be2', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'It can be learned that in Iowa，_____. [A] wind is a widely used energy source风能是一种被广泛使用的能源 [B] wind energy has replaced fossil fuels风能已经取代了化石燃料 [C] tech giants are investing in clean energy科技巨头正在投资清洁能源 [D] there is a shortage of clean energy supply清洁能源供应存在短缺 12', null, 'A', '选项A正确。原文明确提到爱荷华州“风力发电机星罗棋布”（wind turbines dot the fields），且风
电占全州发电量的36%（provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation），说明风能已被广泛利
用。
选项B错误。文中未提及风能“完全取代”化石燃料（replaced fossil fuels），仅强调其占比高，且特朗普
仍主张发展化石燃料。
选项C片面。科技巨头（如微软）因清洁能源可用性被吸引（attracted by clean energy），但“投资清洁
能源”这一主动行为未被明确说明。
选项D与原文矛盾。文中指出清洁能源充足（availability of clean energy），而非短缺。
方法二：非限制性定语从句中找复现词wind，复现词是重点讨论对象，所以更有可能放在选项的主语位
置，排除CD，句子不是讨论tech giants，也不是a shortage of clean energy supply，然后B有fossil
fuel非限制性定从里没有这个意群的重现。
真题演练七
13
①The power and ambition of the giants of the digital economy is astonishing - Amazon has just
announced the purchase of the upmarket grocery chain Whole Foods for $13.5bn, but two years ago
Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have
any physical product at all. ②What WhatsApp offered Facebook was an intricate and finely detailed
web of its users'' friendships and social lives.
According to Paragraph 1, Facebook acquired WhatsApp for its____.
A. digital products数字产品
B. user information用户信息
C. physical assets实体资产
D. quality service优质服务
答案及解析
14
正确答案：B（user information）
选项B正确。原文明确提到，WhatsApp为Facebook提供的是“用户友谊和社交生活的复杂而
精细的网络”（an intricate and finely detailed web of its users'' friendships and social lives），这属
于用户信息范畴。选项A（digital products）错误。WhatsApp本身是数字服务，但收购原因并非其
“产品”，而是用户数据。选项C（physical assets）错误。文中强调WhatsApp“没有任何实体产品”
（doesn''t have any physical product at all）。选项D（quality service）错误。服务质量未被提及，
收购核心是用户社交关系数据。
真题演练八
15
Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to
invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty. This has been dubbed “quarterly capitalism.”', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 11, true, 49, null),
  ('2975e136-c2a0-5d0f-abf4-b6ce1682c893', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to', '[{"key": "A", "text": "obtain more financial support 获取更多财政资金支持 / 拿到更多经费补贴"}, {"key": "B", "text": "boost their student enrollments促进招生"}, {"key": "C", "text": "improve their teaching quality 提升教学质量"}, {"key": "D", "text": "meet local governments'' needs 满足地方政府的需求"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 17, true, 51, null),
  ('11da5c03-fa7c-585c-a852-f6bcfe9d006a', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to A. obtain more financial support ✅（正确答案）', null, '', '原文第5段指出，公立大学的州政府拨款部分取决于毕业率和学生留存率等指标，而“grade forgiveness”通过
提高GPA间接提升了这些数据，从而帮助学校获得更多财政支持。
B. boost their student enrollments B 混淆留存率 retention 和招生率 enrollments，偷换概念；
C. improve their teaching quality（与教学质量无关，无中生有）
D. meet local governments'' needs（词义偷换：把政府考核要求篡改为政府自身需求（needs），原文无依据；
推导过远：属于多层间接推论，不是政策直接带来的结果；
片面狭隘：只能勉强贴合半句内容，无法完整对应段落里高校的两大收益点，偏离段落总起句 “满足高校自
身需求” 的核心。）
非限制性定语从句总结
21', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 20, true, 52, null),
  ('4445d9af-fee7-5630-a364-e0ca48107353', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 21, true, 53, null),
  ('7004e061-7a8b-5255-8469-bea8527dc3a8', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'but two years ago Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have any physical product at all.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 21, true, 54, null),
  ('c7df8ae4-d219-5b8f-8cf8-ea4b71b9e153', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 21, true, 55, null),
  ('4ecd6e06-4098-5c85-9ee9-4f57cdf26039', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'they''ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another big concern for colleges. 非限制性定语从句要不就是考点本身，要不就是跟考点相关的信息，因此考试时要重视非限制性定语从句阅读 特殊的非限制性定语从句 特殊的非限定性定语从句 23 【which】 例子：So the centers need to be well air-conditioned，which uses even more energy 因此这些场馆需要配备制冷效果良好的空调，而这又会消耗更多能源。 as：which 只能后置，不能放句首；as 引导这类评论性定语从句， 三处位置全能放：句首、句中插入、句尾； 24 These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and increase allegiance to the firm，which Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and increase allegiance to the firm，as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out. as在句尾 as插在句中 These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and, as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out, increase allegiance to the firm. As Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out,these terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and increase allegiance to the firm as在句首 真题演练十 25 ①These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and, as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out, increase allegiance to the firm. ②“You have the importation of terminology that historically used to be associated with non-profit organizations and religious organizations: terms like vision, values, passion, and purpose,” said Khurana.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 21, true, 56, null),
  ('283704f6-5241-5dd9-9db1-811ed51ea3a6', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Khurana believes that the importation of terminology aims to ______. [A] revive historical terms复兴旧时用语 [B] promote company image提升企业形象 [C] foster corporate cooperation促进企业内部合作 [D] strengthen employee loyalty增强员工忠诚度 重要的复现词 Khurana把公司术语和非盈利机构术语进行对比 26 ①These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and, as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out, increase allegiance to the firm. ②“You have the importation of terminology that historically used to be associated with non-profit organizations and religious organizations: terms like vision, values, passion, and purpose,” said Khurana. ① 表层形式：同根 / 同范畴上下义词 二者上位词都是 organization（组织 / 机构），属于同一语义场范畴复现（都是 “独立法人”）。 ② 深层逻辑：反向对立复现（Contrast Repetition） 内核是一组盈利属性反义词： firm = for-profit organization 营利性组织 non-profit organization 非营利性组织 原文作者恰恰利用二者属性对立做对比论证： 27 解题步骤：定位关键信息：原文提到，这些术语旨在"infuse work with meaning"（为工作注入意义），并引 用Khurana教授的观点指出，它们能"increase allegiance to the firm"（增强对公司的忠诚度）。 后文进一步说明，这些术语（如vision, values, passion, purpose）传统上与非营利组织和宗教组织相关， 暗示其情感号召力。选项匹配：[D] strengthen employee loyalty：直接对应原文"increase allegiance to the firm"（allegiance ≈ loyalty）。术语如"purpose, passion"等旨在激发员工情感认同，从而提升忠诚度。 [A] revive historical terms（复兴历史术语）：原文仅提到术语的"历史关联性"，未提及"复兴"这一目的，属 于过度引申。[B] promote company image（提升公司形象）：原文未提及对外宣传或形象塑造，偏离核心。 [C] foster corporate cooperation（促进企业合作）"合作"（cooperation）与原文"忠诚"（allegiance）概念 不符。 介词提前的定语从句 介词提前的定语从句 29 This is the hospital in which I was born 主句：This is the hospital 简单句： I was born in the hospital 阅读方法——切分成两个单句 30 【例子1】reading becomes the default state from which you temporarily surface to take care of business. 简单句1： reading becomes the default state 翻译：阅读成为默认状态 简单句2： you temporarily surface(from the default state) to take care of business (from the default state) 翻译：你暂时从默认状态切换出来处理事务 【例子2】Rare is the household in which the division of labor is so clinically and methodically laid out. 简单句1：Rare is the household（倒装句） 翻译：这样的家庭实属罕见 简单句2：the division of labor is so clinically and methodically laid out in the household 翻译：在家庭中，劳动分工的安排是（像医学般）仔细，精准且有条不紊。 总：很少的家庭，劳动分工的安排是（像医学般）仔细，精准且有条不紊。 真题演练十一 31 ①A new study suggests that contrary to most surveys, people are actually more stressed at home than at work. ② At work, people pretty much know what they’re supposed to be doing: working, making money, doing the tasks they have to do in order to draw an income. ③The bargain is very pure: Employee puts in hours of physical or mental labor and employee draws out life-sustaining moola.④On the home front, however, people have no such clarity. ⑤Rare is the household in which the division of labor is so clinically and methodically laid out. ⑥There are a lot of tasks to be done, there are inadequate rewards for most of them.', null, 'D', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 25, true, 57, null),
  ('e7ef4ae1-43b2-5b37-b592-bbef36329c4d', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The home front differs from the workplace in that______. [A] family labor is often adequately rewarded家庭劳动往往能得到充分的回报 [B] home is hardly a cozier working environment家几乎算不上是更舒适的工作场所 [C] household tasks are generally more motivating家务事通常更能激发人的积极性 [D] division of labor at home is seldom clear-cut家庭内部的分工很少界限分明 32', null, '及解析', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 31, true, 58, null),
  ('07135ab4-8399-5fb4-9a6f-5b0ce1f2fce6', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '正确答案：D 解题步骤：定位关键信息（题干：home front vs. workplace）：工作场所（workplace）： 原文②段：人们清楚自己该做什么（"know what they''re supposed to be doing"），即任务明确、回报 直接（"draw an income"）。家庭环境（home front）： 原文③段：家庭中分工不明确（"no such clarity"），且劳动分配"rarely clinically and methodically laid out"（很少像临床手术般精确规划）。家庭任务奖励不足（"inadequate rewards"）。 题目： What is commonly regarded as the cause of grade inflation? 原文只说 more stressed（心理压力更大） 压力大 = 精神内耗、任务边界模糊、付出没回报； B 选项偷换成 cozier（物理环境舒适度） cozy 指房间舒适度、硬件环境、体感惬意度，全文自始至终零提及房屋环境、居家硬件好不好。 这属于概念范畴偷换，不是简单脑补，是出题人典型的 “近义词概念嫁接陷阱”。 完型填空—定语从句 完型填空-定语从句 34 情况一：根据限定关系解题 【例题1】 The ____that I live in faces north. A cat B environment C house D address 【例题2】Even ....... homeless individuals manage to find a _____that will give them three meals a day and a place to sleep at night, .......... A lodging(出租的宿舍） B shelter （收容所） C dwelling（公寓，住宅） D house（房子） 完型填空-定语从句 35 情况二：根据先行词和关系连词解题 【例题1】 I live in a house whose_____is brown [A] leg [B] roof [C] hair [D] address 【例题2】Second, some paper checks（纸质支票） have the advantage that they provide receipt（ 发票，收据）, something that many consumers are unwilling to _____ [A] give up（放弃） [B] take over（接管） [C] bring back（带回来） [D] pass down（传承） 36', null, '及解析', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 32, true, 59, null),
  ('e3595b29-c719-5889-aac7-2a5841702e32', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '答案：C. house。 解析：句子主干是“The ______ faces north”（某物朝北），需要填入一个能“朝北”且与“I live in” （我住在其中）搭配的名词。A. cat（猫）：不符合逻辑，我不能住在猫里。B. environment（环境）：通常不与“live in” 直接搭配，且“环境朝北”语义不通。D. address（地址）：地址是抽象概念，无法“朝北”。C. house（房子）：唯一合理 选项，房子有朝向，且“I live in the house”语义通顺。', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 36, true, 60, null),
  ('0f422e7e-146e-5e45-882b-9628b19df702', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '答案：B. shelter', null, '', '句子描述无家可归者寻找能提供“三餐和住宿”的地方，需选择与“救助”相关的词汇。A. lodging：通常指付费的临
时住所，无家可归者可能无法负担。C. dwelling 和 D. house：均指长期住宅，与“临时救助”语境不符。B. shelter（收容
所）：专门为无家可归者提供免费食宿的场所，完全匹配题意。', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 36, true, 61, null),
  ('b1cb44e1-4d14-592f-9c4b-5e9ef6434de4', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '答案：B. roof', null, '', '需填入一个属于“房子”且能是“棕色”的部分。A. leg（腿）：房子没有腿。C. hair（头发）：房子没有头发。D.
address（地址）：地址是抽象信息，无颜色属性。B. roof（屋顶）：房子的屋顶可以有颜色，符合逻辑。', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 36, true, 62, null),
  ('406bfb9f-8d3c-52e1-80af-825c86ed0223', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '答案：A. give up', null, '', '句意为“纸质支票提供收据，这是许多消费者不愿______的功能”。B. take over 和 D. pass down：与“收据”无关，
语义不匹配。C. bring back：消费者不会“带回”收据，逻辑不通。A. give up（放弃）：消费者不愿放弃收据这一功能，
符合常理（如电子支付可能无收据）。
Recap
37
Thanks.', '英语2/长难句-定从2 (1).pdf', 36, true, 63, null),
  ('972c53de-2635-583e-a1ad-72b14fcf4d14', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '绝对明确 2. 相对明确 作用 修饰限定先行词，不能省 略，影响表意 补充说明先行词，可以省 略，不影响 非限制性定语从句总结 6', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 5, true, 64, null),
  ('ef617c45-9c0b-548b-952f-54d737cff17c', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.【绝对明确】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 6, true, 65, null),
  ('f7b44e9d-7a86-53d5-8af0-bf3969fc198c', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'but two years ago Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have any physical product at all.【绝对明确】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 6, true, 66, null),
  ('46d78554-7c46-5103-b04e-68d280aaa3e1', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty. 【相对明确-短期投资者】', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 6, true, 67, null),
  ('411e6d01-16f5-524c-b466-af1a748e2d12', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'they''ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another big concern for colleges. 【相对明确-学费】 非限制性定语从句阅读方式-分清主从句，意群，谁跟谁并列 7 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers. 在爱荷华州，这一表态并未得到广泛认同。该州田野上风力发电机星罗棋布，风电已占全州发电量的 36%。科技巨头（如微软）正因清洁能源的充沛供应而纷纷选址于此，为其数据中心提供动力支持。 第一步：找出所有动词 did not play，dot，provide，are being attracted， to power 第二步：非谓语动词词组=起点+终点（前） 起点：to do；doing；done 终点=下一个标点符号前；下一个连接词前；下一 个动词前 to power their data centers. 第三步：一个连词+搭配一个动词+终点（下一个 标点符号；下一个连接词；下一个动词）', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 6, true, 68, null),
  ('7c86af3e-ab97-505f-9079-2429482d183b', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'where wind turbines .... electricity generation', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 7, true, 69, null),
  ('cbb80f89-dcb5-5c07-8aea-1439fcf1b5dc', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'where tech giants.... clean energy 解决三个问题①形式中判断是非限制性定从 ②分清楚句子层次，主 从句，谁跟谁并列③复现意群 ④学有余力者，翻译 8 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 问题一：复现意群？？？ 上下义复现【概括+具体】：2组词 同义复现/替换：1组词 指代复现：1组 非限制性定从，大于8个字，所以翻译时候独立成句 9 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 上下义复现【概括+具体】：clean energy-wind；tech giants-Microsoft 同义复现/替换：provide electricity=to power 指代复现： tech giants-their 翻译：非限制性定从，大于8个字，所以翻译时候独立成句 10 But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation /and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy/ to power their data centers. 但这一说法在爱荷华州并不受许多民众认可。在该州，风力发电机遍布田野，风能供应全州 36% 的 发电量；也正是在该州，充足的清洁能源吸引了微软这类科技巨头入驻，为它们的数据中心供 电。 真题演练六：风能供电，为科技巨头数据中心供电，与这个方向更 贴近 11 President Trump has underlined fossil fuels——especially coal——as the path to economic growth. In a recent speech in Iowa，he dismissed wind power as an unreliable energy source. But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 7, true, 70, null),
  ('06a44900-919a-567e-9a58-a82fdbd6832a', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'It can be learned that in Iowa，_____. [A] wind is a widely used energy source风能是一种被广泛使用的能源 [B] wind energy has replaced fossil fuels风能已经取代了化石燃料 [C] tech giants are investing in clean energy科技巨头正在投资清洁能源 [D] there is a shortage of clean energy supply清洁能源供应存在短缺 12', null, 'A', '选项A正确。原文明确提到爱荷华州“风力发电机星罗棋布”（wind turbines dot the fields），且风
电占全州发电量的36%（provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation），说明风能已被广泛利
用。
选项B错误。文中未提及风能“完全取代”化石燃料（replaced fossil fuels），仅强调其占比高，且特朗普
仍主张发展化石燃料。
选项C片面。科技巨头（如微软）因清洁能源可用性被吸引（attracted by clean energy），但“投资清洁
能源”这一主动行为未被明确说明。
选项D与原文矛盾。文中指出清洁能源充足（availability of clean energy），而非短缺。
方法二：非限制性定语从句中找复现词wind，复现词是重点讨论对象，所以更有可能放在选项的主语位
置，排除CD，句子不是讨论tech giants，也不是a shortage of clean energy supply，然后B有fossil
fuel非限制性定从里没有这个意群的重现。
真题演练七
13
①The power and ambition of the giants of the digital economy is astonishing - Amazon has just
announced the purchase of the upmarket grocery chain Whole Foods for $13.5bn, but two years ago
Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have
any physical product at all. ②What WhatsApp offered Facebook was an intricate and finely detailed
web of its users'' friendships and social lives.
According to Paragraph 1, Facebook acquired WhatsApp for its____.
A. digital products数字产品
B. user information用户信息
C. physical assets实体资产
D. quality service优质服务
答案及解析
14
正确答案：B（user information）
选项B正确。原文明确提到，WhatsApp为Facebook提供的是“用户友谊和社交生活的复杂而
精细的网络”（an intricate and finely detailed web of its users'' friendships and social lives），这属
于用户信息范畴。选项A（digital products）错误。WhatsApp本身是数字服务，但收购原因并非其
“产品”，而是用户数据。选项C（physical assets）错误。文中强调WhatsApp“没有任何实体产品”
（doesn''t have any physical product at all）。选项D（quality service）错误。服务质量未被提及，
收购核心是用户社交关系数据。
真题演练八
15
Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to
invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty. This has been dubbed “quarterly capitalism.”', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 11, true, 71, null),
  ('fdc88ab7-635d-5157-a21b-8f35745c4fe1', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'mcq', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to', '[{"key": "A", "text": "obtain more financial support 获取更多财政资金支持 / 拿到更多经费补贴"}, {"key": "B", "text": "boost their student enrollments促进招生"}, {"key": "C", "text": "improve their teaching quality 提升教学质量"}, {"key": "D", "text": "meet local governments'' needs 满足地方政府的需求"}]'::jsonb, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 17, true, 73, null),
  ('5e415db9-72e5-566f-ba7e-fcde46804366', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'According to Paragraph 5, grade forgiveness enables colleges to A. obtain more financial support ✅（正确答案）', null, '', '原文第5段指出，公立大学的州政府拨款部分取决于毕业率和学生留存率等指标，而“grade forgiveness”通过
提高GPA间接提升了这些数据，从而帮助学校获得更多财政支持。
B. boost their student enrollments B 混淆留存率 retention 和招生率 enrollments，偷换概念；
C. improve their teaching quality（与教学质量无关，无中生有）
D. meet local governments'' needs（词义偷换：把政府考核要求篡改为政府自身需求（needs），原文无依据；
推导过远：属于多层间接推论，不是政策直接带来的结果；
片面狭隘：只能勉强贴合半句内容，无法完整对应段落里高校的两大收益点，偏离段落总起句 “满足高校自
身需求” 的核心。）
