21', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 20, true, 74, null),
  ('a0e6414b-672e-5b5c-b1fd-34f48d3dc1bc', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'But that message did not play well with many in Iowa，where wind turbines dot the fields and provide 36 percent of the state’s electricity generation and where tech giants like Microsoft are being attracted by the availability of clean energy to power their data centers.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 21, true, 75, null),
  ('926bed3d-97c6-57c4-9262-9af9ca088d06', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'but two years ago Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn''t have any physical product at all.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 21, true, 76, null),
  ('62a7bddc-eb2d-58ed-b1b5-570ead35ae31', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Transient investors, who demand high quarterly profits from companies, can hinder a firm’s efforts to invest in long-term research or to build up customer loyalty.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 21, true, 77, null),
  ('cf575ca1-3fcd-52b3-b081-7da3dc73e569', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'they''ve gotten a better value for their tuition dollars, which is another big concern for colleges. 非限制性定语从句要不就是考点本身，要不就是跟考点相关的信息，因此考试时要重视非限制性定语从句阅读 特殊的非限制性定语从句 特殊的非限定性定语从句 23 【which】 例子：So the centers need to be well air-conditioned，which uses even more energy 因此这些场馆需要配备制冷效果良好的空调，而这又会消耗更多能源。 as：which 只能后置，不能放句首；as 引导这类评论性定语从句， 三处位置全能放：句首、句中插入、句尾； 24 These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and increase allegiance to the firm，which Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and increase allegiance to the firm，as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out. as在句尾 as插在句中 These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and, as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out, increase allegiance to the firm. As Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out,these terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and increase allegiance to the firm as在句首 真题演练十 25 ①These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and, as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out, increase allegiance to the firm. ②“You have the importation of terminology that historically used to be associated with non-profit organizations and religious organizations: terms like vision, values, passion, and purpose,” said Khurana.', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 21, true, 78, null),
  ('5dbbcce1-0fc5-5375-a296-2b87f162f140', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'Khurana believes that the importation of terminology aims to ______. [A] revive historical terms复兴旧时用语 [B] promote company image提升企业形象 [C] foster corporate cooperation促进企业内部合作 [D] strengthen employee loyalty增强员工忠诚度 重要的复现词 Khurana把公司术语和非盈利机构术语进行对比 26 ①These terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning and, as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out, increase allegiance to the firm. ②“You have the importation of terminology that historically used to be associated with non-profit organizations and religious organizations: terms like vision, values, passion, and purpose,” said Khurana. ① 表层形式：同根 / 同范畴上下义词 二者上位词都是 organization（组织 / 机构），属于同一语义场范畴复现（都是 “独立法人”）。 ② 深层逻辑：反向对立复现（Contrast Repetition） 内核是一组盈利属性反义词： firm = for-profit organization 营利性组织 non-profit organization 非营利性组织 原文作者恰恰利用二者属性对立做对比论证： 27 解题步骤：定位关键信息：原文提到，这些术语旨在"infuse work with meaning"（为工作注入意义），并引 用Khurana教授的观点指出，它们能"increase allegiance to the firm"（增强对公司的忠诚度）。 后文进一步说明，这些术语（如vision, values, passion, purpose）传统上与非营利组织和宗教组织相关， 暗示其情感号召力。选项匹配：[D] strengthen employee loyalty：直接对应原文"increase allegiance to the firm"（allegiance ≈ loyalty）。术语如"purpose, passion"等旨在激发员工情感认同，从而提升忠诚度。 [A] revive historical terms（复兴历史术语）：原文仅提到术语的"历史关联性"，未提及"复兴"这一目的，属 于过度引申。[B] promote company image（提升公司形象）：原文未提及对外宣传或形象塑造，偏离核心。 [C] foster corporate cooperation（促进企业合作）"合作"（cooperation）与原文"忠诚"（allegiance）概念 不符。 介词提前的定语从句 介词提前的定语从句 29 This is the hospital in which I was born 主句：This is the hospital 简单句： I was born in the hospital 阅读方法——切分成两个单句 30 【例子1】reading becomes the default state from which you temporarily surface to take care of business. 简单句1： reading becomes the default state 翻译：阅读成为默认状态 简单句2： you temporarily surface(from the default state) to take care of business (from the default state) 翻译：你暂时从默认状态切换出来处理事务 【例子2】Rare is the household in which the division of labor is so clinically and methodically laid out. 简单句1：Rare is the household（倒装句） 翻译：这样的家庭实属罕见 简单句2：the division of labor is so clinically and methodically laid out in the household 翻译：在家庭中，劳动分工的安排是（像医学般）仔细，精准且有条不紊。 总：很少的家庭，劳动分工的安排是（像医学般）仔细，精准且有条不紊。 真题演练十一 31 ①A new study suggests that contrary to most surveys, people are actually more stressed at home than at work. ② At work, people pretty much know what they’re supposed to be doing: working, making money, doing the tasks they have to do in order to draw an income. ③The bargain is very pure: Employee puts in hours of physical or mental labor and employee draws out life-sustaining moola.④On the home front, however, people have no such clarity. ⑤Rare is the household in which the division of labor is so clinically and methodically laid out. ⑥There are a lot of tasks to be done, there are inadequate rewards for most of them.', null, 'D', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 25, true, 79, null),
  ('34f9d8f9-0df6-529d-8b94-2476daa09ffe', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', 'The home front differs from the workplace in that______. [A] family labor is often adequately rewarded家庭劳动往往能得到充分的回报 [B] home is hardly a cozier working environment家几乎算不上是更舒适的工作场所 [C] household tasks are generally more motivating家务事通常更能激发人的积极性 [D] division of labor at home is seldom clear-cut家庭内部的分工很少界限分明 32', null, '及解析', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 31, true, 80, null),
  ('88e3eb41-c295-51c4-ace4-14a2520b86ce', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '正确答案：D 解题步骤：定位关键信息（题干：home front vs. workplace）：工作场所（workplace）： 原文②段：人们清楚自己该做什么（"know what they''re supposed to be doing"），即任务明确、回报 直接（"draw an income"）。家庭环境（home front）： 原文③段：家庭中分工不明确（"no such clarity"），且劳动分配"rarely clinically and methodically laid out"（很少像临床手术般精确规划）。家庭任务奖励不足（"inadequate rewards"）。 题目： What is commonly regarded as the cause of grade inflation? 原文只说 more stressed（心理压力更大） 压力大 = 精神内耗、任务边界模糊、付出没回报； B 选项偷换成 cozier（物理环境舒适度） cozy 指房间舒适度、硬件环境、体感惬意度，全文自始至终零提及房屋环境、居家硬件好不好。 这属于概念范畴偷换，不是简单脑补，是出题人典型的 “近义词概念嫁接陷阱”。 完型填空—定语从句 完型填空-定语从句 34 情况一：根据限定关系解题 【例题1】 The ____that I live in faces north. A cat B environment C house D address 【例题2】Even ....... homeless individuals manage to find a _____that will give them three meals a day and a place to sleep at night, .......... A lodging(出租的宿舍） B shelter （收容所） C dwelling（公寓，住宅） D house（房子） 完型填空-定语从句 35 情况二：根据先行词和关系连词解题 【例题1】 I live in a house whose_____is brown [A] leg [B] roof [C] hair [D] address 【例题2】Second, some paper checks（纸质支票） have the advantage that they provide receipt（ 发票，收据）, something that many consumers are unwilling to _____ [A] give up（放弃） [B] take over（接管） [C] bring back（带回来） [D] pass down（传承） 36', null, '及解析', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 32, true, 81, null),
  ('cf0b61ed-9179-5138-843c-3a94fca26feb', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '答案：C. house。 解析：句子主干是“The ______ faces north”（某物朝北），需要填入一个能“朝北”且与“I live in” （我住在其中）搭配的名词。A. cat（猫）：不符合逻辑，我不能住在猫里。B. environment（环境）：通常不与“live in” 直接搭配，且“环境朝北”语义不通。D. address（地址）：地址是抽象概念，无法“朝北”。C. house（房子）：唯一合理 选项，房子有朝向，且“I live in the house”语义通顺。', null, '', '', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 36, true, 82, null),
  ('c4605f63-f7d6-58fa-b469-64aa8eeec5e0', '22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222221', 'short', '答案：B. shelter', null, '', '句子描述无家可归者寻找能提供“三餐和住宿”的地方，需选择与“救助”相关的词汇。A. lodging：通常指付费的临
时住所，无家可归者可能无法负担。C. dwelling 和 D. house：均指长期住宅，与“临时救助”语境不符。B. shelter（收容
所）：专门为无家可归者提供免费食宿的场所，完全匹配题意。', '英语2/长难句-定从2.pdf', 36, true, 83, null)
